                "Deposition_Efficiency_Value": "",
                "Deposition_Efficiency_Units": "",
                "Grain_Size_Value": "",
                "Grain_Size_Units": "",
                "Microstructural_Features": "Deposit had an elemental composition of 18.90 at% Cr, 12.30 at% Ni, 1.96 at% Mo, 2.00 at% Mn, 3.00 at% O, 0.04 at% Al, and 61.80 at% Fe. only the austenite phase (c) was detected presenting a FCC structure without the existence of oxides in the coating. coating was dense and had similar chemical composition as powder, indicating that no significant chemical interactions and no phase transformation occurred during spraying. strong coating bonding due to penetration of steel particles into the al substrate. Higher roughness than He deposit (N2 deposit R=15.8 μm). Observed a presence of many inter-splat voids (pores) and some cracks. Oxides on surface."
            },
            "Notes": "N2. For the nanoindentation test a penetration time of 36s was given which may differ from dwell time. In methods N2 is given as 100 m/s gas flow rate, but is later given as 1000 m/s. I reported 1000 m/s since it makes more sense considering it should be supersonic. Velocity modelling results consider three particle sizes, 15, 28, and 25 μm reported above is 28 μm. 15 μm particles had a velocity of 661 m/s, temperature of 253°C, and η value of 1.03. 35 μm particles had a velocity of 569 m/s, temperature of 375°C, and η value of 1.06."
        },
